data/evidence/audit-queue.csv:103:alharbi2023-baby-foods-saudi-arabia-heavy-metals,Manual Fetch Kimi /06_Infant_Foods_Formula,MFK_occurrence-and-dietary-exposure-assessment-of-heav,f25d37b,2026-05-18T06:39:00Z,audited-codex-promote,PROMOTE,2026-05-19,"v2.0 autonomous manual-fetch skill; Alharbi NS et al. 2023 Food Sci Nutr 11:5270-5282 (DOI 10.1002/fsn3.3485) A-tier SFDA NFMP 2020 occurrence + dietary-exposure study; n=111 commercial Saudi baby foods (39 stage 1 formula + 22 stage 2 formula + 33 cereal-based meals + 17 biscuits) from Riyadh/Jeddah/Dammam (21 domestic + 90 imported); Agilent 7700 ICP-MS with helium CCT after Milestone UltraCLAVE microwave digestion of 0.50 g aliquots in ultrapure 65% HNO3, validated to CSN EN 15763 + BS EN 13804:2013 with recovery 116/106/108% and RSD 6.42/3.28/3.83% for As/Cd/Pb (Table 1); Codex CCCF LB/MB/UB substitution for left-censored data; EDI/THQ/HI/MoE per USEPA + EFSA framework using Saudi MoH 2021 body weights 5.45 kg (0-6 mo) + 8.90 kg (7-12 mo); EXISTING merge-enhance path + DUPLICATE CONSOLIDATION — two prior wiki pages (this page revision 2026-05-12 and original2020-original-a.md revision 2026-05-14, both with raw_handle FM_10494610) consolidated into this canonical cite-key; original2020 cite-key was a manifest text-mining artifact (first_author 'original' from 'ORIGINAL ARTICLE' header; year mis-mined as 2020) which the page itself carried a suggested_cite_key_rename flag for; original2020-original-a.md deleted in the same commit; major enhancements vs prior 2026-05-12 revision — added full LB/MB/UB EDI Table 2 + THQ/HI Table 3 + MoE Table 4 + per-food-group exposure-contribution percentages (As 29.1/9.18/3.32% + Cd 8.08/5.89/2.19% for 7-12 mo + 19.5% As / 21.4% Cd for 0-6 mo formula-only), expanded Methods (UltraCLAVE programme + ICP-MS atomic masses 75/111/208 + RF/gas settings + EN method references + Table 1 method validation), added Kruskal-Wallis + Mann-Whitney pairwise p-values (Cd significant <0.001 formula-vs-cereal-meals + formula-vs-biscuits and 0.007 cereal-meals-vs-biscuits), added reference-value context (USEPA RfDs + EFSA Pb BMDL01 + JECFA Cd PTMI + Pb PTWI withdrawal + IARC classes), corrected As-mean transposition between cereal-based meals (15.5 ug/kg) and biscuits (11.1 ug/kg) present in the retired original2020 page, replaced legacy '## Wiki pages updated on ingest' heading with '## Wiki pages this source may touch', tightened speciation to tAs per CLAUDE.md Part 14 (paper measures total As; iAs RfD applied to total intake is methods-detail simplification not a speciation measurement); manual_fetch_path added pointing at the Manual Fetch Kimi PDF; preserved cite_key + raw_handle FM_10494610 + raw_path + license CC BY 4.0 + evidence_tier A + sample_n 111 + jurisdictions [SA]; frontmatter metals [tAs Cd Pb] + ingredients [infant-formula-powder baby-cereals-dry] + products [infant-formula-powder baby-cereals-dry-rice-based baby-cereals-dry-non-rice teething-and-snacks-rice-based teething-and-snacks-non-rice] (broad scope - paper does not split soy/non-soy or rice/non-rice); routing 7 product-page rows generated 0 unresolved 0 blocking malformed; **note: ingest commit hash f25d37b is the parallel-session mahaffey1975 audit-queue commit — my staged alharbi2023 changes were swept into that commit by a race condition between two concurrent Claude sessions writing to the working tree at the same instant. File changes are correctly captured in git; only the commit message is misattributed. Documented here for traceability.**; subagent verdict PROMOTE all 5 checks clean — Check 1 every numeric value verified verbatim against PDF p.5272-5279 (Table 1 LOD/LOQ + 12 group-metal MB ranges + 8 mean+SD cells + 6 K-W/M-W p-values + 12 EDI cells Table 2 + 16 THQ/HI cells Table 3 + 6 MoE cells Table 4 + 8 exposure-contribution percentages + 5 RfD/BMDL/PTMI reference values + body weights + consumption + sample sizes 39/22/33/17), Check 2 every slug in taxonomy snapshot (metals + ingredients + products + 5 regulations + wiki-pages-this-source-may-touch), Check 3 speciation tAs correct (PDF section 2.2.3 names monitored masses As 75/Cd 111/Pb 208 — no speciation column) + methods faithful + risk-assessment equations match equations 1-5, Check 4 brand-firewall clean (no brand names; paper reports only aggregated category data; instrument/material vendors covered by Exception 2), Check 5 HMTc-firewall clean (Implications report paper's own MoE-below-10 interpretation without proposing thresholds or consumer advisories; no cross-source synthesis); 0 findings to apply (PROMOTE); 1 minor cosmetic ⚠️ from subagent (stage-2 7-scoops parenthetical could clarify per-feed-vs-per-day arithmetic; not a correctness issue, faithful to paper's own awkward phrasing — left as-is); audit verdict PROMOTE with no content changes needed; skipping audit-application commit per skill step 13; [''] | Codex fire audit 2026-05-19: five-check audit clean; no page changes."
