data/evidence/autonomy/manual-fetch-stops-2026-05-30.md:27:**Discover-skill mis-score pattern:** The filename `*-composition-*` was auto-fetched as part of a "camel milk composition" topic sweep alongside the heavy-metals-specific PDFs in the same folder (`afzal2024-camel-milk-heavy-metals.pdf`, `chen2020-camel-milk-heavy-metals.pdf`, etc., which ARE in-scope). The discover-skill scoring should down-weight "composition / diabetes / therapeutic / functional food" review papers when no heavy-metals analyte appears in title, abstract, or keywords. Title keyword "Composition" alone is too noisy; the topic-fit gate should require at least one heavy-metals analyte token (Pb/Cd/As/Hg/Ni/Al/Cr/Sn/Sb/U or "heavy metals" / "trace metals" / "toxic metals" / "metal contamination") in the abstract before auto-fetching.
